1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,340
Listen, practice, speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:18,340
Hello and welcome to Business English Conversations.

3
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:23,700
Hello everyone, and welcome back to the podcast where we practice real English used in the

4
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,780
workplace.

5
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,340
My name is Emma.

6
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:27,700
And my name is David.

7
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:33,980
In this podcast, we help you improve your professional English through natural conversations.

8
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:38,620
Yes, we talk about situations that happen in real business environments,

9
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:46,700
such as meetings, presentations, job interviews, networking, and everyday conversations at work.

10
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:50,300
Today, we are going to discuss a very useful topic.

11
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,500
Our topic today is how to describe your skills in English.

12
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:59,900
This is an important skill because many people need to talk about their abilities.

13
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,380
Especially during job interviews.

14
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:04,140
or performance reviews

15
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:05,900
or networking events

16
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:09,340
sometimes even during casual conversations with colleagues

17
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:12,540
when someone asks what are your strengths

18
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:14,940
or what skills do you have

19
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:18,460
many people feel nervous when answering these questions

20
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:21,660
yes because it can be difficult to talk about yourself

21
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:26,940
but it's important to learn how to explain your skills clearly and confidently

22
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:30,380
in today's conversation we will show you how to do that

23
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:35,740
We will talk about different types of skills, including technical skills, communication

24
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:41,820
skills, and leadership skills. And we will give examples of how to describe them in simple

25
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:48,940
business English. So, let's begin. David, let me ask you a question. Sure. If someone asked you

26
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:54,300
to describe your professional skills, what would you say? That's a good question. Take your

27
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:59,300
Well, I would probably start by talking about my communication skills.

28
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,300
Why communication skills?

29
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:03,300
Because they are very important in my job.

30
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:06,300
What exactly do you do in your job?

31
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:08,300
I work as a marketing manager.

32
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:12,300
That role definitely requires strong communication.

33
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:15,300
Yes, I communicate with many different people every day.

34
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,300
Such as?

35
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:22,300
My team members, clients, designers, and sometimes company executives.

36
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:25,300
That's a lot of communication.

37
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:29,300
Yes, and each conversation requires a slightly different style.

38
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:31,300
That's very true.

39
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:35,300
For example, when I talk to clients, I focus on understanding their needs.

40
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:37,300
That's an important skill.

41
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:40,300
Yes, active listening is a big part of communication.

42
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:44,300
Many people forget that listening is also a skill.

43
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:48,300
Exactly. Communication is not only about speaking.

44
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:51,300
It's also about understanding others.

45
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,460
and asking the right questions.

46
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:58,420
So how would you describe your communication skills in a professional way?

47
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:00,660
I might say something like this.

48
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:01,460
Go ahead.

49
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:07,540
Quote, I have strong communication skills and experience working with cross-functional teams.

50
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,940
That sounds very professional.

51
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:10,740
Thank you.

52
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:12,580
What else might you say?

53
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:16,100
I might add that I'm good at presenting ideas clearly.

54
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:19,460
Presentations are very important in marketing.

55
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:22,900
Yes, I often present campaign strategies to clients.

56
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:25,740
Are you comfortable speaking in front of groups?

57
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:28,260
Yes, I've developed that skill over time.

58
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:31,300
Many people feel nervous about public speaking.

59
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,220
That's true.

60
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:35,260
How did you improve your presentation skills?

61
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:36,200
Practice.

62
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,420
That's usually the best answer.

63
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:40,180
The more presentations I gave,

64
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:42,060
the more confident I became.

65
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:45,060
That's a great example of skill development.

66
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:46,160
Exactly.

67
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:48,940
Now, let me ask you another question.

68
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:49,940
Sure.

69
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:52,460
What about technical skills?

70
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:55,280
Those are also very important.

71
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:57,420
Especially in many modern jobs.

72
00:03:57,420 --> 00:04:01,580
Yes, technology plays a big role in almost every industry.

73
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:04,980
What technical skills are important in your job?

74
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:06,880
Data analysis is one of them.

75
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:10,000
How do you use data analysis in marketing?

76
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,720
We analyze customer behavior and campaign performance.

77
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:16,820
That helps you understand what works and what doesn't.

78
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:17,820
Exactly.

79
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:20,540
So how would you describe that skill?

80
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:26,180
I might say something like, I have strong analytical skills and experience using marketing

81
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:27,980
analytics tools.

82
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:30,180
That sounds very professional.

83
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:31,180
Thank you.

84
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:35,020
Another technical skill I have is digital advertising management.

85
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:36,980
What does that involve?

86
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:39,500
Managing online advertising campaigns.

87
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,540
On platforms like social media?

88
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:44,940
Yes, social media platforms and search engines.

89
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:48,540
That requires both creativity and technical knowledge.

90
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:49,540
Exactly.

91
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:52,100
Now let me share some of my skills.

92
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:53,700
I would love to hear them.

93
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:58,940
As a project manager, one of my strongest skills is organization.

94
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:00,020
That makes sense.

95
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:03,900
My job requires managing multiple tasks and deadlines.

96
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,500
That can be very challenging.

97
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:10,460
Yes, especially when working on several projects at the same time.

98
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:11,940
How do you stay organized?

99
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:15,380
I use project management tools and detailed planning.

100
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:17,140
That's a good strategy.

101
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:21,260
I also create clear timelines for each project.

102
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:23,460
Timelines help everyone stay on track.

103
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:24,460
Exactly.

104
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:28,020
So how would you describe your organizational skills in English?

105
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:33,980
I might say I have strong organizational and project management skills.

106
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:36,060
That sounds clear and professional.

107
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:37,060
Thank you.

108
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:39,100
Do you also have leadership skills?

109
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:42,780
Yes, leadership is another important skill in my role.

110
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,700
How do you demonstrate leadership?

111
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:49,420
I guide the team and make sure everyone understands their responsibilities.

112
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:51,660
That's essential for project success.

113
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:55,100
I also help resolve problems when challenges appear.

114
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:58,060
Conflict resolution is an important leadership skill.

115
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:01,820
Yes, sometimes team members have different opinions.

116
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:04,540
And a good leader helps the team move forward.

117
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:05,580
Exactly.

118
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:08,620
How would you describe your leadership skills in English?

119
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:15,500
I might say I have experience leading cross-functional teams and coordinating complex projects.

120
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,140
That's a great way to describe leadership experience.

121
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:19,100
Thank you.

122
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:22,060
Another important skill is problem solving.

123
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:23,420
Absolutely.

124
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:26,780
Employers value people who can solve problems effectively.

125
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,540
Can you give an example?

126
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:29,180
Sure.

127
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,060
Go ahead.

128
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:34,780
Quote, in one project, our advertising campaign was not performing well.

129
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:36,060
What happened?

130
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:39,180
The engagement rate was much lower than expected.

131
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:41,420
That must have been frustrating.

132
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:45,180
Yes, but we analyzed the data and identified the problem.

133
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:46,780
What was the issue?

134
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:49,340
The target audience was too broad.

135
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:51,180
So what did you do?

136
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:54,300
We refined the audience and adjusted the message.

137
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:56,220
Did that improve the results?

138
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:59,500
Yes, the campaign performance improved significantly.

139
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:02,140
That's a great example of problem solving.

140
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:03,260
Exactly.

141
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:07,820
Now, when describing your skills, examples are very helpful.

142
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:10,460
Yes, because they show real experience.

143
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:13,980
Instead of just saying, I am good at problem solving,

144
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:17,020
you can explain a situation where you solved a problem.

145
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,340
That makes your answer stronger.

146
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:20,700
And more convincing.

147
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:24,140
Another useful skill to describe is teamwork.

148
00:07:24,140 --> 00:07:27,580
Yes, teamwork is essential in almost every job.

149
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:30,380
Very few people work completely alone.

150
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:31,500
That's true.

151
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:33,940
most projects involve collaboration.

152
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:36,820
So how would you describe teamwork skills?

153
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:40,740
You could say, I work well in team environments.

154
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:43,480
Or I enjoy collaborating with colleagues

155
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,260
to achieve shared goals.

156
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:47,460
That's a very good sentence.

157
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:48,260
Thank you.

158
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:52,940
Another useful phrase is cross-functional collaboration.

159
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:55,580
That means working with different departments.

160
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:56,580
Exactly.

161
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:59,780
Such as marketing, finance, and operations.

162
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:02,940
Those teams often need to cooperate.

163
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,760
Yes, especially in large organizations.

164
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:08,460
Let's talk about another important skill.

165
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:09,280
Which one?

166
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,820
Time management.

167
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:12,940
That is extremely important.

168
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:16,140
Especially when you have many responsibilities.

169
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:18,340
How do you manage your time effectively?

170
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:22,860
I prioritize tasks based on urgency and importance.

171
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:24,300
That's a smart strategy.

172
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:28,140
I also break large tasks into smaller steps.

173
00:08:28,140 --> 00:08:30,620
That makes projects feel more manageable.

174
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:31,540
Exactly.

175
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:34,820
So how would you describe your time management skills?

176
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:38,900
I might say I have strong time management skills

177
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:41,180
and consistently meet deadlines.

178
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,620
That's a great statement.

179
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:45,940
Employers always appreciate reliability.

180
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:47,060
Absolutely.

181
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:51,100
Another skill many people talk about is adaptability.

182
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:54,620
Yes, especially in today's fast changing work environment.

183
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:57,180
Companies often go through changes.

184
00:08:57,180 --> 00:09:00,780
New technologies, new strategies, new markets.

185
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:03,620
So employees need to adapt quickly.

186
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:05,820
How would you describe adaptability?

187
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:11,180
You could say, I'm adaptable and comfortable working in dynamic environments.

188
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:12,620
That's very professional.

189
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:13,820
Thank you.

190
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:16,700
Let's also talk about learning skills.

191
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:19,340
Lifelong learning is very important today.

192
00:09:19,340 --> 00:09:22,620
Technology and industries change quickly.

193
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:25,140
So professionals must continue learning.

194
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:27,540
How do you usually learn new skills?

195
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:30,340
I take online courses and attend workshops.

196
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:31,940
That's a great habit.

197
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:34,180
I also learn a lot from colleagues.

198
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:37,060
Learning from others is very valuable.

199
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:40,340
Yes, experience sharing helps everyone grow.

200
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:42,740
How would you describe your learning ability?

201
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:44,740
I might say something like,

202
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:48,420
I'm a quick learner and always eager to develop new skills.

203
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:50,580
That's a very positive statement.

204
00:09:50,580 --> 00:09:51,300
Thank you.

205
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:54,500
Before we finish, let's review a few useful phrases.

206
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:56,140
Good idea.

207
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:59,220
Here are some examples you can use when describing your skills.

208
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:01,900
I have strong communication skills.

209
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:05,060
I have experience working with cross-functional teams.

210
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:08,460
I'm highly organized and detail-oriented.

211
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:11,860
I have strong analytical and problem-solving skills.

212
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:15,620
I'm comfortable managing multiple projects at the same time.

213
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:19,100
I'm adaptable and open to learning new technologies.

214
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:24,360
These phrases can help you sound confident and professional, especially during interviews

215
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:26,360
or professional conversations.

216
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:30,080
Before we end today's podcast, we have a question for you.

217
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:32,480
Yes, we would love to hear from you.

218
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:35,080
What are your three strongest skills?

219
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,960
Try to describe them in English.

220
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:40,840
You can say something like, one of my strongest skills is...

221
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,800
I also have experience in...

222
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:46,440
Another important skill I have is...

223
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:49,880
Practicing these sentences will help you improve your business English.

224
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:54,520
And it will also prepare you for job interviews and professional conversations.

225
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,460
Thank you so much for listening today.

226
00:10:56,460 --> 00:11:01,200
We hope this conversation helps you feel more confident when talking about your skills.

227
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,480
Keep practicing English every day.

228
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:08,640
And remember, your skills are valuable, so don't be afraid to talk about them.

229
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:09,640
From both of…

230
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:10,640
Hi everyone.

231
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:13,200
We are very happy you are here with us today.

232
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,200
Hello everyone.

233
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,360
My name is David.

234
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:16,960
And my name is Erica.

235
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:20,400
Welcome back to our Business English Conversation channel.

236
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:26,160
On this channel, we help you practice English for work, interviews, and professional situations.

237
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,260
That's right.

238
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:31,960
Business English is very important if you want to communicate at work and describe your

239
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,960
skills.

240
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:37,320
Many jobs require you to talk about your abilities in interviews and meetings.

241
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:43,320
So today, we will practice how to describe your skills in simple and professional English.

242
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:47,140
We will use easy phrases so you can understand and practice.

243
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:52,320
If you enjoy learning with us, please like this video and subscribe to our channel.

244
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:54,920
It really helps us make more lessons for you.

245
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:55,920
Thank you so much.

246
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:58,000
Let's start our conversation.

247
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Good idea.

248
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,520
Mia, how are you today?

249
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,800
I am good, thank you.

250
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,040
A little busy, but that is fine.

251
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:07,800
Being busy usually means you are working on important tasks.

252
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:10,920
Yes, I was working on a small project this morning.

253
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,280
That sounds interesting.

254
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,960
What kind of project was it?

255
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,560
It was a marketing project.

256
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:18,920
We were planning ideas for an advertisement campaign.

257
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:22,000
Marketing projects require creativity and planning.

258
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,160
Exactly.

259
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:26,440
Marketing is about communication and understanding customers.

260
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:28,520
That reminds me of today's topic.

261
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:32,800
Yes, we are talking about how to describe your skills in English.

262
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:37,960
Describing skills is important in job interviews and professional situations.

263
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:41,560
Employers want to know what you can do and how you can help their company.

264
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:45,620
So let's practice simple ways to explain your abilities.

265
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:46,620
Good idea.

266
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:48,520
Let's start with the basic question.

267
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:49,960
What is a skill?

268
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:55,160
A skill is something you can do well because of practice or experience.

269
00:12:55,160 --> 00:13:00,400
Skills can be technical, like using a computer, or soft skills, like communication.

270
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:04,380
Technical skills are abilities related to tools or technology.

271
