529
00:26:38,140 --> 00:26:41,260
and that any potential risks are addressed early.

530
00:26:41,260 --> 00:26:45,020
That sounds like a role that requires strong organizational skills.

531
00:26:45,020 --> 00:26:51,100
It definitely does. I rely on planning tools, progress reports, and regular check-in meetings

532
00:26:51,100 --> 00:26:53,180
to keep everything organized.

533
00:26:53,180 --> 00:26:56,540
How do you usually start coordinating a new project?

534
00:26:56,540 --> 00:27:02,180
The first step is usually defining the project objectives and creating a clear timeline.

535
00:27:02,180 --> 00:27:07,740
I work with the team to break the project into smaller tasks and assign responsibilities.

536
00:27:07,740 --> 00:27:10,220
That helps make the project more manageable.

537
00:27:10,220 --> 00:27:11,420
Exactly.

538
00:27:11,420 --> 00:27:16,700
Large projects can feel overwhelming, so dividing them into smaller tasks makes it easier

539
00:27:16,700 --> 00:27:19,640
for everyone to stay focused and productive.

540
00:27:19,640 --> 00:27:23,720
Have you always been comfortable with project coordination, or did you develop that skill

541
00:27:23,720 --> 00:27:24,800
over time?

542
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:27,560
I definitely developed it over time.

543
00:27:27,560 --> 00:27:31,960
Early in my career, I focused more on completing individual tasks.

544
00:27:31,960 --> 00:27:37,060
But as I gained more experience, I started taking on responsibilities that involved coordinating

545
00:27:37,060 --> 00:27:38,920
larger initiatives.

546
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:41,200
That's often how professional growth happens.

547
00:27:41,200 --> 00:27:47,040
Yes, and I've also learned a lot by observing experienced managers and project leaders, watching

548
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:51,640
how they organize work and communicate with teams has been very valuable.

549
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:54,920
Another skill people often talk about is adaptability.

550
00:27:54,920 --> 00:27:57,160
Would you say that's also one of your strengths?

551
00:27:57,160 --> 00:28:01,760
Yes, I think adaptability is very important in today's workplace.

552
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:05,880
Things change quickly, especially when you're working on multiple projects.

553
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:09,200
Can you give an example of how you've demonstrated adaptability?

554
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:10,200
Sure.

555
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:14,720
There was a time when one of our major projects suddenly changed direction because

556
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:20,040
the client introduced new requirements. We had already completed a significant portion

557
00:28:20,040 --> 00:28:23,840
of the work, so we had to adjust our plans quickly.

558
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:25,400
That must have been challenging.

559
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:31,480
It was, but instead of focusing on the disruption, our team focused on finding solutions. We

560
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:37,440
reorganized our tasks, updated the timeline, and prioritized the new requirements.

561
00:28:37,440 --> 00:28:39,960
And were you able to deliver the project successfully?

562
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:45,320
Yes, we were. The project was completed a little later than originally planned, but the client was

563
00:28:45,320 --> 00:28:50,360
satisfied because we adapted to their needs and delivered a high-quality result.

564
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:53,480
That's a great example of adaptability and teamwork.

565
00:28:53,480 --> 00:28:59,800
Exactly. In many workplaces, flexibility and a positive attitude toward change are essential

566
00:28:59,800 --> 00:29:04,760
skills. Another skill that employers often value is leadership. Would you say you have

567
00:29:04,760 --> 00:29:10,840
developed leadership abilities as well? Yes, although I'm still developing that area. Leadership

568
00:29:10,840 --> 00:29:16,200
doesn't always mean managing a large team. Sometimes it simply means taking initiative

569
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:21,480
and helping guide a group toward a common goal. That's a very good definition of leadership.

570
00:29:21,480 --> 00:29:27,240
For example, during team projects I often volunteer to organize meetings, track progress,

571
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:32,360
and help colleagues if they encounter challenges. Those are definitely leadership behaviors.

572
00:29:32,360 --> 00:29:37,440
Yes, and I've noticed that when someone takes responsibility for coordinating efforts,

573
00:29:37,440 --> 00:29:40,640
it helps the entire team work more efficiently.

574
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:45,400
When you describe your skills like this, it becomes much clearer what you actually do and

575
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:47,480
how you contribute to a team.

576
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:48,480
That's true.

577
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:50,840
Simply listing skills isn't enough.

578
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:55,520
It's much better to explain how you use those skills in real situations.

579
00:29:55,520 --> 00:29:59,100
That's a very important point for anyone learning professional English.

580
00:29:59,100 --> 00:30:03,300
When someone asks about your skills, try to describe them with examples from your work

581
00:30:03,300 --> 00:30:04,300
experience.

582
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:05,580
Exactly.

583
00:30:05,580 --> 00:30:10,500
You can talk about challenges you faced, actions you took, and the results you achieved.

584
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:14,020
That makes your explanation more interesting and more persuasive.

585
00:30:14,020 --> 00:30:16,340
I also think confidence plays a role.

586
00:30:16,340 --> 00:30:19,980
Sometimes people feel uncomfortable talking about their own strengths.

587
00:30:19,980 --> 00:30:23,940
That's true, but describing your skills isn't about bragging.

588
00:30:23,940 --> 00:30:28,620
It's simply about explaining what you can contribute to a team or organization.

589
00:30:28,620 --> 00:30:33,140
And when you explain your abilities clearly, it helps others understand your value.

590
00:30:33,140 --> 00:30:34,140
Exactly.

591
00:30:34,140 --> 00:30:39,460
Whether you're applying for a job, collaborating with colleagues, or presenting your ideas,

592
00:30:39,460 --> 00:30:43,700
being able to describe your skills effectively is extremely useful.

593
00:30:43,700 --> 00:30:45,900
Well this has been a really helpful discussion.

594
00:30:45,900 --> 00:30:46,900
I agree.

595
00:30:46,900 --> 00:30:52,220
Hopefully our listeners now feel more confident about talking about their own skills in English.

596
00:30:52,220 --> 00:30:54,780
Thank you all for listening to today's episode.

597
00:30:54,780 --> 00:30:57,620
And remember, the best way to improve your English...

598
00:30:57,620 --> 00:31:01,580
Hello everyone, and welcome back to our English Learning Podcast.

599
00:31:01,580 --> 00:31:06,500
Today we're going to talk about another very important communication skill in English.

600
00:31:06,500 --> 00:31:11,480
The topic of today's conversation is how to describe your skills in English.

601
00:31:11,480 --> 00:31:15,240
This is something many people need to do in different situations.

602
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:19,640
You might need to describe your skills during a job interview, when introducing yourself

603
00:31:19,640 --> 00:31:23,860
to colleagues, while networking, or even when writing your resume.

604
00:31:23,860 --> 00:31:25,540
Yes, that's right.

605
00:31:25,540 --> 00:31:30,020
about your skills can sometimes feel uncomfortable, especially for people who are not used to

606
00:31:30,020 --> 00:31:32,060
speaking about their achievements.

607
00:31:32,060 --> 00:31:36,100
Some people feel shy while others are not sure which words to use.

608
00:31:36,100 --> 00:31:41,380
But describing your skills clearly is extremely important because it helps others understand

609
00:31:41,380 --> 00:31:44,340
what you can do and how you can contribute.

610
00:31:44,340 --> 00:31:45,340
Exactly.

611
00:31:45,340 --> 00:31:50,340
And one of the biggest mistakes people make is either saying too little or saying something

612
00:31:50,340 --> 00:31:51,780
too general.

613
00:31:51,780 --> 00:31:57,220
For example, someone might say, I'm good at many things, or I work hard.

614
00:31:57,220 --> 00:32:00,900
While those statements may be true, they don't give enough information.

615
00:32:00,900 --> 00:32:04,420
Yes, and listeners usually want something more specific.

616
00:32:04,420 --> 00:32:09,460
They want to know what you are good at and how you use those skills in real situations.

617
00:32:09,460 --> 00:32:14,220
The good news is that describing your skills in English doesn't require complicated grammar

618
00:32:14,220 --> 00:32:16,340
or advanced vocabulary.

619
00:32:16,340 --> 00:32:20,260
What you really need is clear explanations and examples.

620
00:32:20,260 --> 00:32:25,900
a very good point. When people hear the word skills, they might think only about professional

621
00:32:25,900 --> 00:32:31,460
or technical abilities. But actually, skills can be divided into different categories.

622
00:32:31,460 --> 00:32:36,780
Yes, in many professional environments, people talk about two main types of skills. The

623
00:32:36,780 --> 00:32:42,740
first type is technical skills. These are abilities related to specific tools, technologies

624
00:32:42,740 --> 00:32:50,020
or professional knowledge. For example, programming, data analysis, graphic design, or accounting.

625
00:32:50,020 --> 00:32:53,740
And the second type is what many people call soft skills.

626
00:32:53,740 --> 00:32:58,860
These are personal abilities that help you work with others and manage tasks effectively.

627
00:32:58,860 --> 00:33:00,020
Exactly.

628
00:33:00,020 --> 00:33:06,060
Soft skills include things like communication, teamwork, problem-solving, time management,

629
00:33:06,060 --> 00:33:07,300
and leadership.

630
00:33:07,300 --> 00:33:11,740
These skills are extremely valuable because they influence how well you collaborate with

631
00:33:11,740 --> 00:33:13,100
other people.

632
00:33:13,100 --> 00:33:16,300
Let's imagine someone asks you a simple question.

633
00:33:16,300 --> 00:33:17,740
What are your strengths?

634
00:33:17,740 --> 00:33:21,420
Many English learners suddenly feel nervous when they hear that question.

635
00:33:21,420 --> 00:33:26,540
Yes, because it feels like you are being asked to promote yourself, but there is a very simple

636
00:33:26,540 --> 00:33:28,500
way to answer this kind of question.

637
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:34,540
You can start by naming a skill, then explaining it, and finally giving a short example.

638
00:33:34,540 --> 00:33:36,140
That's a very useful structure.

639
00:33:36,140 --> 00:33:40,460
First, you mention the skill, then you describe how you use it.

640
00:33:40,460 --> 00:33:41,460
Exactly.

641
00:33:41,460 --> 00:33:45,820
For example, someone might say, one of my strongest skills is communication.

642
00:33:45,820 --> 00:33:51,200
I enjoy explaining ideas clearly and making sure everyone on the team understands the

643
00:33:51,200 --> 00:33:52,200
plan.

644
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:54,080
That answer is clear and natural.

645
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:57,640
It doesn't sound exaggerated, but it still shows confidence.

646
00:33:57,640 --> 00:34:01,500
Yes, and confidence is important when describing your skills.

647
00:34:01,500 --> 00:34:05,520
You don't need to sound arrogant, but you should speak in a way that shows you believe

648
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:07,200
in your abilities.

649
00:34:07,200 --> 00:34:10,600
Another good example could be related to organization.

650
00:34:10,600 --> 00:34:13,720
Someone might say, I have strong organizational skills.

651
00:34:13,720 --> 00:34:18,440
I like planning tasks and creating schedules, so projects stay on track.

652
00:34:18,440 --> 00:34:23,080
That's a great example. It shows how the skill is used in a real situation.

653
00:34:23,080 --> 00:34:28,920
When listeners hear this, they can imagine the person working in an organized and structured way.

654
00:34:28,920 --> 00:34:32,520
Let's talk about another common skill, problem solving.

655
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:36,520
Many employers value people who can solve problems effectively.

656
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:39,400
Yes, and someone might describe this skill by saying,

657
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:43,560
I enjoy solving problems and finding practical solutions.

658
00:34:43,560 --> 00:34:49,280
When challenges appear, I like analyzing the situation and identifying the best way forward.

659
00:34:49,280 --> 00:34:52,160
That explanation sounds thoughtful and professional.

660
00:34:52,160 --> 00:34:55,520
It also shows a positive attitude toward challenges.

661
00:34:55,520 --> 00:34:56,520
Exactly.

662
00:34:56,520 --> 00:34:58,640
And that's something many companies appreciate.

663
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:05,120
They want employees who see challenges as opportunities to improve things rather than obstacles.

664
00:35:05,120 --> 00:35:08,480
Another important skill that many people mention is teamwork.

665
00:35:08,480 --> 00:35:11,680
Yes, teamwork is essential in many workplaces.

666
00:35:11,680 --> 00:35:13,440
Someone might describe it like this,

667
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:15,520
I work well in team environments.

668
00:35:15,520 --> 00:35:17,680
I enjoy collaborating with others

669
00:35:17,680 --> 00:35:20,800
and sharing ideas to achieve common goals.

670
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:22,320
That's a great sentence.

671
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:26,320
It shows that the person values cooperation and communication.

672
00:35:26,320 --> 00:35:29,360
In those qualities often lead to stronger results

673
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,880
because teams function better

674
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:33,520
when people respect and support each other.

675
00:35:33,520 --> 00:35:35,120
Now let's talk about something

676
00:35:35,120 --> 00:35:37,280
that many learners struggle with.

677
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:41,520
finding the right balance between being confident and being humble.

678
00:35:41,520 --> 00:35:46,240
That's an excellent point. When describing your skills, it's important to sound confident,

679
00:35:46,240 --> 00:35:49,600
but also realistic. Instead of saying something like,

680
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:55,280
I'm the best at everything, it's better to focus on specific strengths and explain them calmly.

681
00:35:55,280 --> 00:35:59,440
Yes, because exaggerated statements can sound less believable.

682
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:02,160
Clear examples are much more convincing.

683
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:04,640
Exactly. For example, instead of saying,

684
00:36:04,640 --> 00:36:07,600
I'm amazing at leadership. Someone might say,

685
00:36:07,600 --> 00:36:13,360
I enjoy leading small teams and helping people stay motivated while we work towards our goals.

686
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:16,000
That sounds much more natural and professional.

687
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:20,480
Yes, and it allows the listener to understand the person's leadership style.

688
00:36:20,480 --> 00:36:26,080
Another useful strategy when describing skills is connecting them to past experiences.

689
00:36:26,080 --> 00:36:31,120
When you mention something you did in the past, it helps demonstrate the skill in action.

690
00:36:31,120 --> 00:36:33,600
That's true. For example, someone could say,

691
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:36,160
One of my strengths is time management.

692
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:39,400
In my previous role, I often handled multiple projects

693
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:42,720
at the same time, so I learned how to prioritize tasks

694
00:36:42,720 --> 00:36:43,760
effectively.

695
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:46,160
That explanation gives real context.

696
00:36:46,160 --> 00:36:49,360
It shows that the skill was developed through experience.

697
00:36:49,360 --> 00:36:52,520
Yes, an experience makes the skill more believable.

698
00:36:52,520 --> 00:36:56,040
People tend to trust examples more than simple statements.

699
00:36:56,040 --> 00:36:58,520
Let's also talk about creativity.

700
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:01,040
Creativity is valuable in many fields,

701
00:37:01,040 --> 00:37:03,200
not only in art or design.

702
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:09,940
That's right. Creativity can also appear in problem-solving, innovation, and idea generation.

703
00:37:09,940 --> 00:37:16,080
Someone might say, I enjoy thinking creatively in exploring new approaches when solving problems.

704
00:37:16,080 --> 00:37:19,920
That sentence shows openness to new ideas and flexibility.

705
00:37:19,920 --> 00:37:25,560
Exactly. Flexibility is another important skill in today's fast-changing environments.

706
00:37:25,560 --> 00:37:29,240
Many workplaces require employees to adapt quickly.

707
00:37:29,240 --> 00:37:34,240
So someone might describe that skill by saying, I'm adaptable and comfortable learning new

708
00:37:34,240 --> 00:37:36,840
tools or processes when necessary.

709
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:42,040
Yes, and that kind of attitude shows that the person is willing to grow and develop.

710
00:37:42,040 --> 00:37:46,600
Speaking of growth, another good skill to mention is the ability to learn quickly.

711
00:37:46,600 --> 00:37:47,920
Absolutely.

712
00:37:47,920 --> 00:37:52,360
Someone might explain it like this, I'm a fast learner and I enjoy developing new

713
00:37:52,360 --> 00:37:55,080
skills whenever I have the opportunity.

714
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:57,000
That's a very positive statement.

715
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:59,400
It shows curiosity and motivation.

716
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:03,600
Yes, and curiosity often leads to continuous improvement.

717
00:38:03,600 --> 00:38:08,840
Another useful idea when describing your skills is to keep your language simple.

718
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:13,900
Many learners think they need to use complicated vocabulary, but clear language is usually

719
00:38:13,900 --> 00:38:15,400
more effective.

720
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:16,400
That's true.

721
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:19,560
Simple sentences are easier for listeners to understand.

722
00:38:19,560 --> 00:38:24,400
When your message is clear, people focus on your ideas instead of your grammar.

723
00:38:24,400 --> 00:38:28,000
when you feel comfortable with the structure, you can speak more naturally.

724
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:34,560
Yes, practice is the key. The more you practice describing your skills, the easier it becomes.

725
00:38:34,560 --> 00:38:39,800
A great exercise is to choose three or four skills that represent you well and practice

726
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:41,480
explaining them out loud.

727
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:46,880
Exactly. For example, someone might practice saying, I'm very organized, I communicate

728
00:38:46,880 --> 00:38:49,960
clearly, and I enjoy working in teams.

729
00:38:49,960 --> 00:38:53,640
Then they can add short explanations or examples for each skill.

730
00:38:53,640 --> 00:38:59,540
Yes, and after practicing a few times, the explanation begins to feel natural instead of memorized.

731
00:38:59,540 --> 00:39:05,680
Another helpful tip is to listen to how professionals describe their skills in interviews or presentations.

732
00:39:05,680 --> 00:39:08,280
You can learn many useful phrases that way.

733
00:39:08,280 --> 00:39:12,840
That's a great idea. Observing others can give you inspiration and confidence.

734
00:39:12,840 --> 00:39:17,880
Before we finish today's episode, let's remind our listeners of something important.

735
00:39:17,880 --> 00:39:22,840
Everyone has valuable skills, even if they sometimes forget to recognize them.

736
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:29,640
Yes, that's very true. Skills come from experiences, education, hobbies, and personal interests.

737
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:34,340
When you take time to reflect on what you do well, it becomes easier to talk about it.

738
00:39:34,340 --> 00:39:39,940
And when you can describe your skills clearly in English, you open many opportunities for yourself.

739
00:39:39,940 --> 00:39:45,540
Exactly. Good communication helps people understand your strengths and your potential.

740
00:39:45,540 --> 00:39:48,540
Thank you, everyone, for listening to today's conversation.

741
00:39:48,540 --> 00:39:52,620
We hope this discussion helps you feel more confident the next time you talk about your

742
00:39:52,620 --> 00:39:54,300
skills in English.

743
00:39:54,300 --> 00:39:58,020
Keep practicing, keep learning, and keep speaking English.

744
00:39:58,020 --> 00:40:02,060
And we'll see you again in the next episode of our English Learning Podcast.
